       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>59-year-old Meghalaya man returns to Class 10 exams</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Meghalaya</span> <span>#Education</span> <span>#Class 10 Exams</span></div>
       <p>A 59-year-old man from Meghalaya has returned to academic pursuit, currently preparing for his Class 10 examinations. This move comes 37 years after he originally dropped out of the school system, according to the Indian Express.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/59-year-old-meghalaya-man-returns-to-class-10-exams.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the report does not detail his specific career path or the motivation behind his decision to re-enroll after nearly four decades, his return highlights an ongoing commitment to completing his secondary education at this stage in his life. The case serves as a notable instance of adult education and late-stage academic ambition within the state.</p><p>What to watch: Further updates on the examination results and his performance in the upcoming Class 10 board papers.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately reflects the provided source material.</p>
