       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Akhilesh Yadav Calls for Unity in Rajya Sabha Elections</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Samajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav has described the upcoming Rajya Sabha elections as a &quot;time for coming together,&quot; signaling a potential reconciliation with former party members. The SP has already nominated Ram Gopal Yadav and Reliance executive Dhanraj Parimal Nathwani for the polls.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/akhilesh-yadav-calls-for-unity-in-rajya-sabha-elections.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Party leaders indicate the SP may field a third candidate, raising the possibility of a contest and cross-voting. Currently, the BJP-led alliance is positioned to win seven of the 10 available seats in Uttar Pradesh, while the SP, supported by Congress, is projected to secure two.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political situation and the upcoming Rajya Sabha elections based on the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/rajya-sabha-elections-time-for-coming-together-akhilesh-yadav/article71536816.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
