     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>CEC Gyanesh Kumar Protests Erupt in Delhi, Mumbai; 1,100 Detained in Capital</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Politics</span> <span>#Elections</span> <span>#Protests</span> <span>#Awards</span></div>
       <p>Protests against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar have intensified across India, with significant demonstrations reported in Delhi and Mumbai. According to India Today, over 1,100 political and student activists were detained by Delhi Police during earlier demonstrations in the national capital. The unrest in Mumbai is being led by the Citizens Justice Party (CJP), founded by Abhijeet Dipke, which organized a gathering at Shivaji Park in Dadar despite the absence of formal police permission.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/cec-gyanesh-kumar-protests-erupt-in-delhi-mumbai-1100-detain.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The CJP pressed three principal demands at the Shivaji Park venue: the resignation of CEC Gyanesh Kumar, the freezing of the 2025 electoral list, and complete transparency in the appointment of future election chiefs. Large crowds, including youths and first-time voters from various parts of Maharashtra, gathered holding national tricolours and placards. While security forces maintained a heavy presence at the site, the organization has planned further agitations across six other cities leading up to an indefinite demonstration at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi by late October.</p><p>In a separate development highlighted in the same source material, calls have mounted to confer India's highest peacetime gallantry award, the Ashok Chakra, on Captain Smit Machchhar, the Flydubai pilot who foiled a hijack attempt. Shiv Sena MP Milind Deora wrote to Prime Minister Narendra Modi on behalf of Eknath Shinde, urging that the civilian aviator be considered for the honour. Deora drew parallels with Neerja Bhanot, who was awarded the Ashok Chakra after the 1986 Pan Am hijack, noting that Captain Machchhar’s actions saved more than 170 passengers. The decision remains subject to evaluation by the central government and the Ministry of Defence.</p><p>What to watch: The indefinite demonstration planned at Jantar Mantar by late October and the central government’s decision on the Ashok Chakra award.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively combines reporting on the protests with the additional details regarding the pilot's potential award, maintaining clear attribution.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-in-delhi-and-mumbai-cjp-demands-resignation-ytvd-3008240-2026-10-02?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
