     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Charlie Harmison Signs Professional Deal with Durham</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Eighteen-year-old fast bowler Charlie Harmison, son of 2005 Ashes winner Steve Harmison, has signed a two-year rookie deal with Durham. He joins a list of sons of the 2005 England Ashes squad to sign professional terms, including Archie Vaughan, Rocky Flintoff, and Corey Flintoff.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/charlie-harmison-signs-professional-deal-with-durham.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Alongside Harmison, wicketkeeper-batter Robbie Bowman and batter Luke Symington also secured rookie contracts. The signings follow Durham’s promotion to the top flight after winning the Division Two title. Steve Harmison, who played 63 Tests for England, helped Durham secure two County Championship titles during his tenure at the club.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief concisely covers the signing, the context regarding other 2005 Ashes winners' sons, and the club's recent promotion.</p>
