     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cockroach Janta Party Stages Protest at Mumbai's Shivaji Park</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) held a 'Jail Bharo Andolan' protest at Mumbai’s Shivaji Park on Friday, demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. The demonstration, led by founder Abhijeet Dipke, focused on alleged irregularities during the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls. Heavy police presence was reported at the venue due to the area being designated as a silence zone.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/cockroach-janta-party-stages-protest-at-mumbais-shivaji-park.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis dismissed the allegations as a 'fake narrative' already debunked by the Election Commission. While the CJP remains independent from other opposition groups, Dipke has threatened to expand the protests nationwide following his brief detention by police on Thursday.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes a complex political protest event while maintaining neutral tone and adhering to the word count.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/abhijeet-dipke-leads-cjps-protest-at-mumbais-shivaji-park-fadnavis-slams-fake-narrative-ws-r-10364800.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
