     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Congo Ebola Death Toll Surpasses 4,000 Amid Treatment Struggles</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Congo’s ongoing Ebola outbreak has reached 4,018 deaths, accounting for nearly half of the 8,300 confirmed cases recorded since May 2026. Efforts to contain the virus are hampered by funding shortages, staff strikes, and the destruction of critical infrastructure, including a key transit centre burned by soldiers in Ituri province.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/congo-ebola-death-toll-surpasses-4000-amid-treatment-struggl.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>UN coordinator Julien Harneis warned that losing treatment centers stalls recovery efforts and denies patients essential care. The crisis was further complicated when a Médecins Sans Frontières aid worker was evacuated to the Netherlands after contracting the rare Bundibugyo virus while working in the region.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and concise summary of the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ebola-treatment-centre-was-burned-down-as-death-toll-in-congo-passes-4000/article71537063.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
