       <h1>Congo Ebola outbreak death toll passes 4,000</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ebola</span> <span>#Congo</span> <span>#Public Health</span> <span>#Outbreak</span></div>
       <p>Authorities in Congo announced that the ongoing Ebola outbreak has recorded more than 4,000 deaths, according to Phys.org. The health officials stated that they are struggling to contain the spread of the virus amidst the rising mortality figures. The report highlights the severity of the crisis as the death toll crosses the 4,000 mark. No specific new cases, treatment strategies, or international response details were provided in the source summary beyond the struggle to contain the spread.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/congo-ebola-outbreak-death-toll-passes-4000.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: Updates on containment efforts and case numbers.</p>
