     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by BBC World, The Hindu World">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Cornell Students Demand Action Amid Anger Over Alleged 2024 Gang Rape</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#World</span> <span>#Education</span> <span>#Cornell University</span> <span>#Student Protests</span></div>
       <p>Students at Cornell University are demanding drastic changes following the resurfacing of allegations concerning an alleged gang rape in 2024. During an emotional student assembly on Thursday, students voiced profound frustration, with one stating, &quot;We're absolutely ashamed of the events that happened on campus.&quot; The investigation into the incident has cast a &quot;dark cloud&quot; over the Ivy League campus, stirring anger, concern about fraternity culture, and a backlash against the university's handling of the situation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/cornell-students-demand-action-amid-anger-over-alleged-2024-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The accuser, identified anonymously as Jane Doe, filed a civil lawsuit against Cornell on September 16, claiming she was drugged and raped at a fraternity house two years ago. She alleged that Cornell failed to protect her or adequately punish the men involved, dubbed the &quot;Cornell Seven.&quot; The university has agreed to an independent investigation and defended its prior handling, stating it conducted an &quot;extensive investigation&quot; over several months, adhering to federal civil rights law, which resulted in &quot;expulsions and suspensions.&quot; However, it cites legal limitations for not publicly disclosing specific disciplinary outcomes.</p><p>New York Governor Kathy Hochul announced shortly after Thursday's assembly that she had appointed state attorney general Letitia James as special prosecutor, citing a &quot;lost faith&quot; in Tompkins County District Attorney Matthew Van Houten, who had initially concluded evidence did not meet the legal threshold for charges but reopened a criminal investigation last week. Students like undergraduate Sophia Riley Sim expressed that they &quot;deserve to know that our institution values our safety more than its reputation.&quot;</p><p>A &quot;Justice for Survivors&quot; protest is scheduled for October 5, with flyers across campus calling for action against alleged rape culture. Organizers are demanding Cornell expel and revoke degrees of alleged perpetrators, rewrite sexual assault punishment policies, initiate an external investigation of the university, and mandate prevention training for campus police. Freshman Eliana Dolven-Miller expressed being &quot;very disgusted to be here,&quot; while Eeshaan Chaudhuri, the student assembly chair, affirmed the campus &quot;stood with victims of sexual violence.&quot; A faculty member described the mood on campus as &quot;dismal,&quot; noting this was not the first time a fraternity group had faced problems.</p><p>What to watch: The &quot;Justice for Survivors&quot; protest on October 5 and the ongoing investigation led by special prosecutor Letitia James.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively covers the key aspects of the Cornell University situation, including the student assembly, the special prosecutor, and the protest plans.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm0e3ed1er1yo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC World</a></li><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/students-protest-cornells-response-to-gang-rape-complaint/article71549035.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
