       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Cyclist Ronan Auge in induced coma after Tour of Langkawi crash</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>French cyclist Ronan Auge has been placed in a medically induced coma following a crash during stage six of the Tour of Langkawi in Malaysia. The 22-year-old was transported to a hospital after sustaining serious injuries during the UCI ProSeries event.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/cyclist-ronan-auge-in-induced-coma-after-tour-of-langkawi-cr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>His team, Unibet Red Roses, stated that Auge is currently in stable, non-life-threatening condition. His accident follows a series of recent incidents in professional cycling, including the death of British rider Fin Tarling and the hospitalization of American Ezra Caudell.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and incorporates all relevant details provided in the source text.</p>
