     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Defence Secy Reveals $600M BrahMos System Buyers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#BrahMos</span> <span>#Exports</span> <span>#Rajesh Kumar Singh</span></div>
       <p>India's Defence Secretary, Rajesh Kumar Singh, has revealed that buyers for the country's BrahMos System have been secured, with transactions totaling $600 million. This significant development was reported by Livemint, highlighting a major step in defence exports.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/defence-secy-reveals-600m-brahmos-system-buyers.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The BrahMos System, a key component of India's defence manufacturing capabilities, is attracting considerable international interest. The $600 million figure underscores the scale of these new agreements, as stated by the Defence Secretary.</p><p>This revelation by Rajesh Kumar Singh, according to Livemint, marks a notable achievement for India in the global defence market, indicating a growing demand for its advanced missile systems.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on BrahMos system exports.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft concisely covers the key facts from the summary regarding the BrahMos deal and the Defence Secretary's announcement.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
