       <h1>Dhaval Patel Warns Indian Students on US Master's Costs, H-1B Challenges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#US Education</span> <span>#Indian Students</span> <span>#H-1B Visa</span></div>
       <p>Dhaval Patel has issued a warning to Indian students considering a master's degree in the United States, citing the significant financial outlay involved. A US master's degree is reported to cost $100,000.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/dhaval-patel-warns-indian-students-on-us-masters-costs-h-1b-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Patel's cautionary advice, highlighted by The Times of India, specifically addresses the challenges Indian students may face concerning job prospects after graduation. He also pointed out difficulties related to the H-1B visa process.</p><p>The warning underscores the importance for prospective students to thoroughly evaluate both the high costs and potential post-study hurdles in the US. This aims to ensure informed decision-making before committing to overseas education.</p><p>What to watch: Further analysis on US job market and visa policies for international students.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source's key points regarding the financial and visa-related risks of US study for Indian students.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
