     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-06 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Education Ministry Announces Rs 5.4 Crore Innovation Challenge</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Innovation</span> <span>#Funding</span></div>
       <p>The Education Ministry has launched a Rs 5.4 crore challenge inviting innovators to submit fresh ideas for the education sector. The call, reported by India Today, urges individuals and teams to apply and compete for funding under the government’s new initiative.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/education-ministry-announces-rs-54-crore-innovation-challeng.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Applicants are expected to present concepts that can enhance learning outcomes, improve infrastructure, or introduce novel technologies in schools and colleges. Details on eligibility criteria, submission deadlines and the application portal are available through the Ministry’s official communication channels.</p><p>The challenge aims to harness grassroots creativity and accelerate the adoption of cutting‑edge solutions across India’s education ecosystem.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and concise report based on the limited source summary provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
