     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Flydubai Boeing 737 MAX‑8 Crisis and Nationwide Protests on Oct 2</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Narendra Modi</span> <span>#Flydubai</span> <span>#Gyanesh Kumar</span> <span>#Delhi Protests</span></div>
       <p>A Flydubai Boeing 737 MAX 8 operating from Dubai to Tel Aviv suffered a severe mid‑air crisis at 34,000 feet when Captain Smit Machhar, an Indian pilot with 17 years of experience, was attacked by his Omani co‑pilot. The altercation caused the aircraft to plunge more than 1,400 feet in 30 seconds, sending the plane into a dangerous descent.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/flydubai-boeing-737-max8-crisis-and-nationwide-protests-on-o.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite serious wounds, Captain Machhar unlocked the cockpit door, enabling crew members and passengers to restrain the attacker and bring the aircraft under control. While on the floor, he said he sensed the rapid descent and recited the Hanuman Chalisa for strength. He later spoke from the hospital with Prime Minister Narendra Modi, who praised the captain’s quick decision‑making and his willingness to put passenger safety above his own life.</p><p>On the same day, the national capital saw mass demonstrations demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over a revision of electoral rolls. The INDIA bloc, student outfits and civil‑society groups converged at Jantar Mantar, where Section 163 was imposed. Delhi Police detained over 1,100 demonstrators, including senior Left leaders M A Baby and Brinda Karat, and escorted them away in buses. Opposition parties – Congress, AAP, Left parties and RJD – accused the Election Commission of removing eligible voters, while the central government defended the poll panel and dismissed the agitation.</p><p>In Mumbai, the Citizens for Justice and Peace (CJP) organised a rally at Shivaji Park in Dadar on Gandhi Jayanti, drawing youth, musicians Vishal Dadlani, Abhijeet Dipke, Saurabh Das and Ashutosh Ranka. Speakers invoked the legacies of Gandhi, Ambedkar and Nehru, criticised government policies, demonetisation and pandemic management, and called for the resignation of CEC Kumar, a freeze on the 2025 electoral list and full transparency in future appointments. A counter‑demonstration also unfolded at the park, while security forces maintained a heavy presence. Organisers announced further agitations in six cities and an indefinite protest at Jantar Mantar by late October.</p><p>What to watch: the impact of the flight incident on aviation safety protocols and the evolving protest movement ahead of the election roll deadline.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the provided source material, covering both the aviation incident and the political protests accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/pm-modi-speaks-to-hero-flydubai-pilot-captain-smit-machhar-protests-on-october-2-ytvd-3008282-2026-10-02?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
