     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Flydubai Captain Praised for Leadership During Mid-Air Stabbing</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Flydubai Captain Smit Machchhar is being hailed for his composure after a co-pilot allegedly stabbed him during flight FZ1073 on September 30, 2026. The incident caused the aircraft to drop 17,400 feet before passengers and crew subdued the attacker. Despite serious injuries, Captain Machchhar prevented passengers from retaliating, urging them to focus entirely on regaining control of the plane.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/flydubai-captain-praised-for-leadership-during-mid-air-stabb.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The flight was safely diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, where the captain underwent emergency surgery. He has since been airlifted to Abu Dhabi for further recovery. Passenger Dr. Maya Peretz praised his leadership, stating his actions were a testament to his humanity and presence of mind under extreme stress.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the incident and the captain's response while maintaining the sourced tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/leave-co-pilot-focus-on-plane-flier-dr-maya-peretz-recounts-injured-captain-smit-machchhars-words-wants-daughter-to-be-like-him-ws-klrt-10364669.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
