       <h1>India Bolsters Air Defence Ecosystem Amid Ukraine's Challenges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Air Defence</span></div>
       <p>India is actively developing a robust air defence ecosystem, contrasting with Ukraine's reported struggles concerning air defence weapons. This development positions India to enhance its defensive capabilities, according to The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/india-bolsters-air-defence-ecosystem-amid-ukraines-challenge.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In a related move to strengthen its air defence infrastructure, the Indian Army recently conducted tests of the Igla-S air defence system. These trials took place in Bikaner, as also reported by The Times of India.</p><p>The ongoing efforts underscore India's commitment to self-reliance and modernization in critical defence sectors.</p><p>What to watch: Further advancements in India's indigenous defence systems.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the available information regarding the Igla-S tests and the broader context provided.</p>
