     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Clinches Asian Games Women's Hockey Gold, Ends 44-Year Wait</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sports</span> <span>#Hockey</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>India secured the Asian Games 2026 women's hockey gold medal on October 2, 2026, defeating World No. 4 China 1-0 in the final held in Kakamigahara. This victory marked the nation's 16th gold at Aichi-Nagoya 2026 and ended a 44-year wait for women's hockey gold at the Asiad, a feat not achieved since 1982. The win also guarantees India direct qualification for the 2028 Olympics in Los Angeles.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/india-clinches-asian-games-womens-hockey-gold-ends-44-year-w.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The sole goal of the match came in the 10th minute of the first quarter from Lalremsiami Hmarzote, who was playing her 200th game for India. A pivotal moment occurred in the second quarter when veteran Indian goalkeeper Savita Punia made an &quot;incredible save&quot; (NDTV Sports fulltext) from a penalty stroke awarded to China. This intervention was highlighted by NDTV Sports as a &quot;stunning penalty save&quot; and a &quot;gold-defining moment.&quot; The Salima Tete-led side then &quot;defended resolutely&quot; through the subsequent quarters to maintain their narrow lead.</p><p>The third quarter saw intense defensive play by India. China was initially awarded a penalty stroke after the ball appeared to touch Navneet Kaur's foot, but the decision was overturned upon referral, resulting in a penalty corner. From this, Indian captain Salima Tete made a &quot;brilliant block&quot; (NDTV Sports fulltext), though she appeared to hurt her hand in the process. China also had a &quot;big chance&quot; at the 12-minute mark of Q3 with a powerful low shot that narrowly missed the target, with no player able to tap it in.</p><p>In the final quarter, with less than 12 minutes remaining, China substituted their goalkeeper for an outfielder in an &quot;all-out attack&quot; attempt. India managed to hold possession, particularly going towards the corner at the 10-minute mark, and denied China &quot;many big chances.&quot; Even in the closing minutes (Q4 13'), Savita Punia made another crucial save after China slammed a shot. India's overall tournament performance was dominant, securing &quot;seven wins in seven matches,&quot; scoring &quot;69 goals,&quot; and conceding &quot;just three goals.&quot; NDTV Sports praised this as a &quot;stunning achievement for Salima Tete, Sjoerd Marijne and co.,&quot; capping a year that also saw India achieve its &quot;best-ever finish&quot; (fifth place) at a Women's Hockey World Cup.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate and comprehensive, covering the key game details and tournament context provided in the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/hockey/india-vs-china-live-score-asian-games-2026-womens-hockey-final-ind-vs-chn-live-match-updates-aichi-nagoya-12129480#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
