       <h1>Jammu &amp; Kashmir Secures First-Innings Lead in Irani Cup</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Jammu &amp; Kashmir achieved a first-innings lead of 41 runs against the Rest of India during their Irani Cup match in Srinagar. Despite struggling at 166 for 8, the team recovered to surpass the Rest of India’s total of 237.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/jammu-kashmir-secures-first-innings-lead-in-irani-cup.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Lone Nasir, batting at No. 10, played a pivotal role by scoring 64 off 58 balls. This late-order resurgence allowed Jammu &amp; Kashmir to post a competitive total, marking a significant turn in the match after fast bowlers had dominated the proceedings on the opening day.</p>
