       <h1>Mahindra and Embraer eye Indian Air Force C‑390 order, plan assembly line in India</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Mahindra</span> <span>#Embraer</span> <span>#C‑390</span> <span>#IAF</span></div>
       <p>Mahindra and Embraer have announced plans to set up a C‑390 Millennium assembly line in India as they target a potential order from the Indian Air Force. The partnership aims to localise production of the medium‑size transport aircraft, aligning with India’s push for indigenous defence manufacturing.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/mahindra-and-embraer-eye-indian-air-force-c390-order-plan-as.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Both firms see the move as a strategic step to meet the IAF’s requirement for modern air‑lift capability, while also expanding Embraer’s footprint in the Indian defence market. Details on the timeline and investment levels were not disclosed.</p><p>What to watch: confirmation of the IAF order and progress on the assembly line establishment.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the provided summary regarding the Mahindra-Embraer partnership for the C-390 assembly line.</p>
