       <h1>Michael Temple Appointed Permanent CEO of Nottinghamshire</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Nottinghamshire has appointed Michael Temple as its permanent chief executive following his tenure as interim leader. Temple, who brings 16 seasons of experience at Trent Bridge, succeeds Richard Kenyon, who recently departed to lead Lancashire after less than one year in the role. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/michael-temple-appointed-permanent-ceo-of-nottinghamshire.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Temple faces a demanding agenda, including overseeing the ongoing pavilion redevelopment at Trent Bridge. Additionally, he must manage the logistical requirements of hosting both the men’s and women’s Ashes series in 2027. His leadership follows the long-standing tenure of Lisa Pursehouse, who served the club for 14 seasons.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all relevant details including the successor, predecessor, and specific upcoming challenges.</p>
