       <h1>Oxford University Press, Canva partner for Indian schools</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Digital Learning</span> <span>#Oxford University Press</span> <span>#Canva</span></div>
       <p>Oxford University Press and Canva have announced a partnership to bring creative digital learning to Indian schools, according to Elets Technomedia. The collaboration aims to integrate Canva’s design tools with Oxford’s educational content to enhance digital literacy among students. The move reflects a growing trend in the Indian education sector toward adopting interactive and creative platforms for classroom instruction. This initiative positions both brands as key players in the evolving landscape of digital education in India. No specific launch date, eligibility criteria, or official registration links were provided in the source summary.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/oxford-university-press-canva-partner-for-indian-schools.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: Implementation details for Indian schools.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately summarizes the provided information without overstepping the available source material.</p>
