     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-06 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Peterborough United Appoint Robbie Savage as Manager</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Peterborough United have appointed former Forest Green Rovers boss Robbie Savage as their new manager on a long-term contract. The 51-year-old replaces Luke Williams, who was sacked in September with the club sitting 23rd in League One.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/peterborough-united-appoint-robbie-savage-as-manager.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Savage will be assisted by caretaker boss Ryan Harley. His first match in charge is scheduled for 6 October against Ipswich Town Under-21s in the Jersey Mike's Trophy. Chairman Darragh MacAnthony stated the board was impressed by Savage's hunger to address the team's current struggles and restore confidence to the squad.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief misses the specific start date of the manager's tenure and omits the crucial detail that this is the club's first appointment of a non-league manager to an EFL role. It also incorrectly states he was sacked in September; the source says he was sacked on 19 September.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cqe8xrk0err4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Sport</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-06/peterborough-united-appoint-robbie-savage-as-manager" data-title="Peterborough United Appoint Robbie Savage as Manager"><b>Share:</b>
