       <h1>Rest of India Trails Jammu and Kashmir by 17 Runs on Day 2 of Irani Cup 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>At the end of Day 2 in the Irani Cup 2026, Rest of India trails Jammu and Kashmir by 17 runs at the Sher-i-Kashmir Stadium in Srinagar. Jammu and Kashmir captain Paras Dogra scored a crucial 75 off 143 balls, sharing a 101-run partnership with Abdul Samad, who added 57 runs. Lone Nasir Muzaffar further contributed with an impressive 64 runs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/rest-of-india-trails-jammu-and-kashmir-by-17-runs-on-day-2-o.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Earlier, left-arm pacer Mukesh Choudhary claimed a five-wicket haul with figures of 5/78 for Rest of India. Akash Deep supported with three wickets for 43 runs, and Mukesh Kumar took two wickets for 84 runs to restrict Jammu and Kashmir's first-innings total.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the current score and provides necessary context from the provided source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/irani-cup-2026-jammu-kashmir-vs-rest-of-india-highlights-review-day-2-9992/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/jammu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jammu</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
