     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rivian Recalls R2 SUV Over Battery Fastener Defect</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Rivian has issued a recall for its R2 SUV after discovering high-voltage battery pack fasteners may be improperly tightened, risking power loss while driving. Approximately 14 vehicles are affected by the defect, which was identified at the company's Normal, Illinois factory on September 17.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/rivian-recalls-r2-suv-over-battery-fastener-defect.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rivian has since reprogrammed its assembly line station to reject improperly torqued fasteners. While the company is not aware of any accidents or injuries related to this issue, it will repair or replace components on affected vehicles as needed. This marks the second recall for the R2 model, which launched earlier this year to help the company reach profitability.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and correctly attributes all provided details from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
