       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Search Underway for Three Boys Swept Away at Rushikonda Beach</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A search operation is ongoing for three 14-year-old boys who went missing after being swept away by strong waves at Rushikonda beach in Visakhapatnam on Friday. The students were part of a group from Madhurawada when they were pulled into deeper water while playing in the sea.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/search-underway-for-three-boys-swept-away-at-rushikonda-beac.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Local police, marine units, community guards, and a scuba-diving team have been deployed to the site to assist in the recovery. Visakhapatnam Commissioner of Police Shankhabrata Bagchi is personally monitoring the rescue efforts as emergency teams continue to search the area.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the incident based on the provided source.</p>
