     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shubman Gill Leads India to 406‑Run Chase, Hails Rohit and Kohli</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Shubman Gill</span> <span>#Virat Kohli</span> <span>#Rohit Sharma</span> <span>#India vs West Indies</span></div>
       <p>India completed a dramatic chase of 406 runs at Barsapara Stadium in Guwahati to win the second ODI against West Indies, after the Caribbean side posted 405. Shubman Gill, who captains the side, played a match‑winning innings of 223 not out, becoming the highest individual scorer of the game and securing an eight‑wicket victory.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/shubman-gill-leads-india-to-406run-chase-hails-rohit-and-koh.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gill praised the senior core of the squad, saying, &quot;I feel extremely lucky. Virat bhai is probably the best ODI batter, and Rohit bhai is the best ODI opener in the world,&quot; adding that their experience is invaluable. Virat Kohli had earlier scored an unbeaten 139 in the first ODI, while Rohit Sharma recorded a century in the second match. In 2026, Rohit has amassed 512 runs in 11 ODIs at 46.54, with two centuries and a best of 138, whereas Kohli has compiled 552 runs in eight ODIs at 78.85, also with two centuries and a top score of 139*.</p><p>Gill’s captaincy is described as consultative; he regularly seeks advice from senior players including KL Rahul and Shreyas Iyer. He explained that he weighs all opinions before making a decision, noting that senior input often highlights considerations he may have missed. Gill’s own 2026 figures are extraordinary: 894 runs from 11 ODIs and 10 innings at an average of 127.71, a strike‑rate of 119.51, and three centuries with five fifties. Over his entire ODI career, he has played 69 matches, scoring 3,712 runs at 65.12, with a strike‑rate above 103, 11 centuries and 20 fifties.</p><p>What to watch: Gill’s ability to blend youthful aggression with senior guidance as India eyes the series decider.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source, including the specific statistics provided for the players' 2026 performance and career totals.</p>
