       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Suno AI Expands Beyond Music to Generate Spoken Words</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tech</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Music</span></div>
       <p>Suno, known for its AI music generation capabilities, is now branching into new territory with the launch of a feature that generates spoken voices. This new functionality allows users to create speech based on provided scripts or prompted descriptions, marking a significant expansion for the platform.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/suno-ai-expands-beyond-music-to-generate-spoken-words.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The speech generation feature is now available in public beta across Suno's web and mobile platforms. This move integrates spoken word capabilities directly into its existing offerings, enhancing its utility for a broader range of creative projects.</p><p>Crucially, the new feature enables users to simultaneously generate voiceovers and accompanying background music. This allows for a cohesive audio production experience, moving beyond just musical compositions to include integrated narrative elements.</p><p>What to watch: Further integrations of speech and music generation on AI platforms.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source's news about Suno's new speech generation feature and its integration with music generation.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1003925/suno-speech-ai-voice-feature-beta-availability" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
