       <h1>UFC Lightweight Bobby Green Targets Historic 2026 Finish</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>UFC lightweight Bobby Green, currently on a four-fight win streak, aims to secure a fifth victory in 2026 when he faces Esteban Ribovics at UFC 332 in Salt Lake City this Saturday. The 40-year-old veteran, who debuted in 2013, is seeking to join an exclusive group of fighters with five wins in a single calendar year.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/ufc-lightweight-bobby-green-targets-historic-2026-finish.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite recent financial success, including a $100,000 performance bonus, Green recently revealed he has been living out of his car while prioritizing the needs of his family and friends. Green clarified he is not &quot;houseless,&quot; noting he has access to support from his social circle while focusing on his career.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate but lacks the necessary context that Green is currently outside the top 15 rankings and reports his financial situation using slightly confusing phrasing.</p>
