     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Times of India, India Today, News18 India">confirmed by 3 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Vande Bharat Express hits 100 kmph on Chenab and Anji bridges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Railways</span> <span>#Kashmir</span> <span>#Vande Bharat</span> <span>#Infrastructure</span></div>
       <p>The maximum permitted speed on the 111-km Shri Mata Vaishno Devi Katra-Banihal railway section has been increased from 75 kmph to 100 kmph. This milestone, announced by Railway Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw, follows the successful testing of the Vande Bharat Express (Train No. 26401/26404) at the higher speed across the Chenab and Anji Khad bridges. The Ministry of Railways approved this enhancement after complying with all prescribed safety conditions in August, according to News18 India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/vande-bharat-express-hits-100-kmph-on-chenab-and-anji-bridge.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Udhampur-Srinagar-Baramulla Rail Link (USBRL) project, which spans 272 kilometres and cost Rs 43,780 crore, connects Kashmir to the Indian Railways network. The route includes 36 tunnels and 943 bridges designed to traverse the Himalayan terrain. To ensure reliability in this earthquake-prone region, the network features seismic dampers and specialized infrastructure.</p><p>The Chenab Rail Bridge stands 359 metres above the riverbed, making it the world's highest railway arch bridge. It is 1,315 metres long and designed to withstand wind speeds of up to 260 kmph. Nearby, the Anji Khad Bridge serves as India's first cable-stayed railway bridge, measuring 725 metres in length and supported by 96 high-tensile cables.</p><p>A specially configured Vande Bharat Express has been introduced to operate on this line. The train is modified for Himalayan winter conditions, featuring heated windshields and insulated toilets to function in temperatures as low as minus 20 degrees Celsius. This upgrade aims to improve service flow, reduce travel times, and increase passenger safety across the region.</p><p>What to watch: Future integration of additional high-speed services across the full USBRL network.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the provided text, capturing both the technical specifications of the bridges and the operational details of the Vande Bharat train.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 3 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/vande-bharat-crosses-worlds-highest-chenab-and-first-cable-stayed-anji-bridges-at-100-kmph-in-historic-milestone-as-katra-banihal-speed-limit-rises-over-a-year-after-inauguration/articleshow/134635017.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/vande-bharat-express-100-kmph-chenab-anji-bridges-katra-banihal-section-ptag-3008139-2026-10-02?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/vande-bharat-crosses-chenab-bridge-at-100-kmph-as-railways-raise-katra-banihal-speed-limit-watch-ws-kl-10365235.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 3 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-06/vande-bharat-express-hits-100-kmph-on-chenab-and-anji-bridge" data-title="Vande Bharat Express hits 100 kmph on Chenab and Anji bridges"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
         <a class="sh-tg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14.4 1.6 1.6 7l3.6 1.2L6 13l2.2-3.1 3.4 2.4 2.8-10.7z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Telegram</a> ·
         <a class="sh-x" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.6 2.6l10.8 10.8M13.4 2.6 2.6 13.4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>X</a> ·
         <a href="#" class="sh-copy"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6.6 9.4a3 3 0 0 0 4.2 0l1.8-1.8A3 3 0 1 0 8.4 3.4L7.5 4.3M9.4 6.6a3 3 0 0 0-4.2 0L3.4 8.4a3 3 0 1 0 4.2 4.2l.9-.9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Copy link</a> ·
