     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>WB NEET UG 2026 Round 3 Choice Filling Commences</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#NEET UG</span> <span>#Counselling</span></div>
       <p>The Round 3 choice filling process for WB NEET UG 2026 counselling has officially begun. This marks a crucial stage for candidates seeking admission through the West Bengal NEET UG counselling process, as reported by The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/wb-neet-ug-2026-round-3-choice-filling-commences.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following the choice filling period, the seat allotment for Round 3 is scheduled to take place on October 8. Candidates are advised to complete their choices within the specified timeframe to be considered for seat allocation.</p><p>This phase is vital for finalising admissions to undergraduate medical courses in West Bengal for the 2026 academic year.</p><p>What to watch: The official seat allotment results on October 8.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the provided source details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
