       <h1>Youth Protesters Demand Resignation of India’s Election Chief Over Voter List Changes</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Election Commission</span> <span>#Gyanesh Kumar</span> <span>#Youth Protests</span> <span>#Voter Rolls</span></div>
       <p>A group of youth demonstrators, described by myRepublica as 'Cockroach' protesters, are preparing to rally again to demand the immediate ouster of India’s election chief. The demonstrations are centered on the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar following controversial revisions to the national electoral rolls. According to ABC News, the protesters are specifically challenging changes made to the voter lists, which they claim have impacted the eligibility of various citizens.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-06/youth-protesters-demand-resignation-of-indias-election-chief.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The movement has gained international attention as student outfits and civil society groups align to question the transparency of the Election Commission. According to reports from both myRepublica and ABC News, the primary objective of the upcoming rally is to force a leadership change at the poll panel to ensure the integrity of future elections. No specific date for the next mass gathering was provided in the initial summaries, but the groups have signaled a continuation of their agitation.</p><p>What to watch: The announcement of specific dates for the next round of youth-led rallies targeting the Election Commission.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and concise summary of the provided text, properly attributing information to the mentioned outlets.</p>
